# Windows CLI Basics

## CLI (Command Line Interface)
- Text-based interface to interact with the system
- Commands are typed instead of using mouse clicks
- Faster and gives more control
- Widely used in cybersecurity and IT

---

# Basic Navigation Commands

## Check Current Directory
- Command: cd
- Shows current working directory

## List Files and Folders
- Command: dir
- Displays files and directories in current location

## Show Hidden Files
- Command: dir /a
- Displays hidden files and folders

---

# Directory Navigation

## Move into Folder
- Command: cd <folder_name>

## Example
- cd Documents

## Move One Level Back
- Command: cd ..

---

# Searching Files

## Command
- dir /s <filename>

## Example
- dir /s task_brief.txt

## Use
- Searches in all subdirectories
- Returns full file path

---

# File Operations

## Read File Content
- Command: type <filename>

## Example
- type task_brief.txt

## Use
- Displays file content in terminal

---

# System Info Commands

## Current Logged-in User
- Command: whoami
- Shows username

## Computer Name
- Command: hostname
- Displays system name

---

# Windows Version Info

## Command
- systeminfo

## Shows
- OS name
- Version
- System type

---

# Network Info

## Command
- ipconfig

## Shows
- IP address
- Network details

---

# Summary Workflow

## Steps
- Navigate → cd
- List → dir
- Search → dir /s
- Read → type
